//! The `--emit-docs` place surface (design 141).
//
// Docs document what the AUTHOR wrote (design 121), and a `borrows` accessor
// reaches the emitter already LOWERED -- the place transform runs inside
// `parse_source` so that registration, inference, monomorphization and codegen
// all see an ordinary generic method. The emitter therefore undoes the rewrite
// for rendering: the synthesized `__window` / `__absent` parameters and the
// `__R` result type parameter are dropped, and `-> __R` goes back to naming the
// PLACE. Without that, a documented subscript would read
// `func []<__R>(&self, i: Int, __window: (&var Int) sync -> __R) sync -> __R`,
// which is the compiler's business and not the reader's.
//
// `sync` is not rendered on a borrows accessor: it is implied by `borrows` (a
// place window may not span a suspension) and the author never writes it.
//
// SL-333 puts BOTH facts a caller needs into the entry. `returns` carries the
// declared window mode -- `&var Int` may be written through, `&Int` may only be
// read -- and `"self"` carries R4's receiver eligibility: `"window"` for an
// accessor whose receiver is borrowed with the window's own flavor (so a `let`
// root may read through it), `"borrows-var"` for an EXCLUSIVE-ONLY one, whose
// body mutates `self` outside the place it lends and which therefore takes the
// receiver exclusively at every use site, reads included. Neither is readable
// off the sigil, which is why reporting the sigil would say the opposite of the
// truth.

// EXPECT: docs
// COMPILE-FLAGS: --emit-docs
// EXPECT-OUTPUT:
// {
//   "schema_version": 4,
//   "modules": [
//     {
//       "name": "doc_emit_borrows",
//       "source": "doc_emit_borrows.saw",
//       "doc": "The `--emit-docs` place surface (design 141).",
//       "items": [
